+Invoke an active tool marked `programmatic: "read-only"` from inside a tool owned by the same extension. The marker controls routing only; Pi still runs the nested call through normal argument validation, tool hooks, permissions, cancellation, and tool execution events. The result is returned to the extension without adding a tool-result message to the conversation.
+
+Pass the current tool call ID as `parentToolCallId`. Pi rejects calls made outside a running parent tool, calls from a different extension, inactive targets, changed target registrations, and nesting beyond one level.
+
+```typescript
+async execute(toolCallId, params, signal) {
+  const target = pi.getAllTools().find((tool) => tool.name === "read");
+  if (!target) throw new Error("read is not registered");
+
+  const nested = await pi.invokeTool(
+    "read",
+    { path: params.path },
+    {
+      parentToolCallId: toolCallId,
+      signal,
+      expectedSourceInfo: target.sourceInfo,
+      expectedRegistrationId: target.registrationId,
+    },
+  );
+
+  return nested.result;
+}
+```
 
